-- title:
--   A sufficient criterion for exceptional-triple cospectrality
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite abelian group. Write $S_+=\{a,a+d,a+d+h\}$, $S_-=\{a,a-d,a-d+h\}$ and $A_\pm(x,y)=1$ if $y-x\in S_\pm$, and zero otherwise. Assume $h\ne0$, $2h=0$, the image of $d$ in $G/\langle h\rangle$ has order exactly three, and $a,d,h$ generate $G$. If either $a,h$ fail to generate $G$ or $|G/\langle h\rangle|$ is even, then
--
--   $$\det(XI-A_+)=\det(XI-A_-).$$
--
--   This gives a sufficient directed spectral criterion.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, https://github.com/alexcour/couret-finite-verifications/blob/65b828d9ffd016ce2a1b05403f303fa5f948c10f/research/correspondants_20261013/lean/CayleyTwoColourParity.lean#L350-L363, lines 350–363; source file SHA-256 d093cc5d0fb31526ef68d4b1d68ee24818c67ebec52adc75170199eecb1ea7a6; theorem Couret.CayleyDoublet.abelianThreeCospectral_of_nongeneration_or_even_quotient

