/-!
COU-20 — parity from finite quotient cardinality (17 October 2026).

The additive parity used by the directed spectral bridge is constructed here.
Let H be generated by h and assume G/H is finite, generated by the images of
a and d, with d+H of odd order. Then a character to ZMod 2 taking a to one
and h to zero exists exactly when G/H has even cardinality. The construction
also kills d. No half-turn or nonzero condition on h is needed for this part.

For the actual finite Cayley adjacency matrices the original nonzero half-turn,
exact order-three quotient and global generation premises are retained.
The disjunction of nongeneration by a,h and even quotient cardinality implies
cospectrality. This is the sufficient direction; the converse spectral
classification, independent human review and priority audit remain separate.
The earlier certified modules and their statements are imported unchanged.
-/

